[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form: \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then we can substitute this into the expression and find the real part.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m The expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m (75 + 117i)(4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m First, let's simplify the expression by multiplying out the terms:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m (75 + 117i)(4\cos\theta + 4i\sin\theta) = 300\cos\theta + 312i\sin\theta + 450i\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m = (300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta) + i(312\sin\theta + 450\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Next, we need to simplify the second term:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
