[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then we can substitute this into the expression and find the real part.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m First, let's express the given expression in terms of \(\theta\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Simplifying the second term:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4} = 24(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)(2 + 3i).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Expanding the second term:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 24(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)(2 + 3i) = 24(2\cos\theta + 3i\cos\theta - 2i\sin\theta + 3\sin\theta) = 24(2\cos\theta + 3\sin\theta + i(3\cos\theta - 2\sin\theta)).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m So the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + 24(2\cos\theta + 3\sin\theta + i(3\cos\theta - 2\sin\theta)).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Expanding the first term:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
