[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m The real part of this expression is \(348\cos\theta - 396\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we need to find the maximum value of the expression \(348\cos\theta - 396\sin\theta\). This can be done by using the fact that the maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). So the maximum value of \(348\cos\theta - 396\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{348^2 + 396^2}\).
