[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m First, we substitute \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Simplifying the expression, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 4(75 + 117i)(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m To simplify the second term, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4} = \frac{96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)}{4} = 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m So the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Combining the real and imaginary parts, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m (300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) + i(300\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta + 36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta) = (324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta) + i(336\cos\theta + 276\sin\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we need to maximize \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). This can be written as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta = 540\left(\frac{324}{540}\cos\theta - \frac{432}{540}\sin\theta\right) = 540\left(\frac{324}{540}\cos\theta - \frac{432}{540}\sin\theta\right) = 540\left(\frac{9}{15}\cos\theta - \frac{12}{15}\sin\theta\right) = 540\left(\frac{3}{5}\cos\theta - \frac{4}{5}\sin\theta\right).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Let \(\cos\phi = \frac{3}{5}\) and \(\sin\phi = \frac{4}{5}\). Then the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 540\left(\cos\phi\cos\theta - \sin\phi\sin\theta\right) = 540\cos(\theta + \phi).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m The maximum value of \(\cos(\theta + \phi)\) is 1, so the maximum value of the real part is \(540 \cdot 1 = 540\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Thus, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(\boxed{540}\).
