[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m The real part of the expression is \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\). To maximize this, we need to maximize the expression \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\). The maximum value of \(a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). So, the maximum value of \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 432^2}\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Thus, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(540\). Let's confirm this with Python code.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m ```python
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m import math
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m # Coefficients
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m a = 324
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m b = -432
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m # Maximum value of a*cos(theta) + b*sin(theta) is sqrt(a^2 + b^2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m max_real_part = math.sqrt(a**2 + b**2)
