[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m First, we substitute \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i) \cdot 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) = 4(75 + 117i)(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Expanding this, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 4(75 \cos \theta + 75i \sin \theta + 117i \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) = 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta + i(75 \sin \theta + 117 \cos \theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m (75 + 117i)z = 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + 4i(75 \sin \theta + 117 \cos \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Next, we consider the term \(\frac{96 + 144i}{z}\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4e^{i\theta}} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4} e^{-i\theta} = (24 + 36i)(\cos \theta - i \sin \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Expanding this, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m (24 + 36i)(\cos \theta - i \sin \theta) = 24 \cos \theta + 24i \sin \theta - 36i \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta = 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta + i(24 \sin \theta - 36 \cos \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta + i(24 \sin \theta - 36 \cos \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Combining both parts, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + 4i(75 \sin \theta + 117 \cos \theta) + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta + i(24 \sin \theta - 36 \cos \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m Separating the real and imaginary parts, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \text{Real part} = 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta = 300 \cos \theta - 468 \sin \theta + 24 \cos \theta + 36 \sin \theta = 324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m We need to maximize \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\). The maximum value of \(a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). So, the maximum value of \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\) is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + (-432)^2} = \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1606671)[0m So, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(540\). The final answer is:
